# {{.ProjectName}}

Qoder plugin scaffold generated by [plugin-kit-ai](https://github.com/777genius/plugin-kit-ai) `init`.

This lane models the observed Qoder plugin bundle shape for portable skills and shared MCP, consumed by both Qoder Desktop and Qoder CLI from the shared `~/.qoder` home.

## Status

- Target lane: `qoder`
- Platform family: `ide_plugin`
- Launcher: not used
- Runtime: native `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, and `Stop` hooks; typed Go handlers are available in `sdk/qoder`

## First Run

```bash
plugin-kit-ai generate .
plugin-kit-ai generate --check .
plugin-kit-ai validate . --platform qoder --strict
```

## Target Files

- `plugin/plugin.yaml`: canonical shared plugin metadata and target list
- `plugin/skills/`: canonical portable skill authored source; `plugin-kit-ai init --extras` pre-seeds a starter and generate mirrors it into plugin-root `skills/`
- `plugin/mcp/servers.yaml`: canonical portable MCP authored source; `plugin-kit-ai init --extras` pre-seeds a starter and generate projects it into managed `.mcp.json` plus `.qoder-plugin/plugin.json#mcpServers`
- `plugin/targets/qoder/hooks/`, `commands/`, and `bin/`: target-native hook configuration, commands, and hook runtimes; `init --extras` seeds examples and generate mirrors them into root `hooks/`, `commands/`, and `bin/`
- root `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`: boundary docs that tell humans and agents to edit only `plugin/`
- `.qoder-plugin/plugin.json`: generated managed Qoder plugin manifest
- `.mcp.json`: generated managed MCP sidecar when portable MCP is authored
- `skills/`: generated managed portable skills

## Install

```bash
qoder plugins install .
```

Then run `/plugins reload` (or restart) in Qoder CLI or Qoder Desktop to apply.

## Current Boundary

- Supported: portable skills and MCP plus target-native hooks, commands, and bundled hook runtimes
- Native hooks and commands stay outside portable component conversion; `agents` and `output-styles` remain future work
- Live SDK hook checks run with `make test-qoder-live` from the tool repository; completed-turn cases require an authenticated Qoder account with chat quota
- The same bundle works for Qoder Desktop and Qoder CLI; only the install path differs (`qoder plugins install` vs Desktop marketplace)
